  "id": "oni_v6",
  "status": "PROPOSED",
  "reference": "NOAA Climate Prediction Center. Oceanic Ni\u00f1o Index (ONI), based on ERSST version 6: \"Oceanic Ni\u00f1o Index (ONI): Historical El Ni\u00f1o / La Ni\u00f1a episodes (1950-Present)\", table \"Cold & Warm Episodes by Season (ERSSTv6)\", and the data file oni.ascii.txt (columns SEAS YR TOTAL ANOM).",
  "url_table_page": "https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/analysis_monitoring/enso/oni/v6/",
  "url_data_file": "https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/data/indices/oni.ascii.txt",
  "url_moved_from": "https://origin.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/analysis_monitoring/ensostuff/ONI_v5.php",
  "locator": "Values: column ANOM of oni.ascii.txt and the one-decimal cell of the v6 table page, rows DJF 2000 to NDJ 2025 (312 seasons). Both sources read again on 2026-11-15 by the L2a orchestrating session: all 312 ANOM values equal the data file byte for byte, and the printed values were extracted from the table page by two independent parsers that agree on every cell of 1950-2025. The check sheet with the 312 rows travels with the signing package.",
  "date_read": "2026-11-15",
  "definition_text": "Warm (red) and cold (blue) periods based on a threshold of +/- 0.5oC for the Oceanic Ni\u00f1o Index (ONI) [3 month running mean of ERSST.v6 SST anomalies in the Ni\u00f1o 3.4 region (5oN-5oS, 120o-170oW)], based on centered 30-year base periods updated every 5 years. For historical purposes, periods of below and above normal SSTs are colored in blue and red when the threshold is met for a minimum of 5 consecutive overlapping seasons.",
  "revision_text": "ONI values may change up to two months after the initial \"real time\" value is posted.",
  "threshold": 0.5,
  "threshold_unit": "degC",
  "min_consecutive_seasons": 5,
  "threshold_met_when": "D240 (2) and D258 of issue #77: the threshold is applied to the one-decimal values printed in the v6 table. Each season of this record carries 'printed', the value as the v6 table prints it, next to 'anom', the two-decimal value of oni.ascii.txt. The threshold reads 'printed' as given; the code holds no rounding rule.",
  "note": "PROPOSED source change, reported: the brief named ONI version 5. On 2026-11-15 the address of the brief (origin.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov ... ONI_v5.php) did not resolve, and the same path on www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov says the page has moved and points to the ERSST version 6 table; it also says that per NWS Public Information Statement 26-05 the Relative Oceanic Ni\u00f1o Index (RONI) is used for official monitoring and prediction. The values of oni.ascii.txt read on that date match the version 6 table and not the version 5 table (for example DJF 2000: ANOM -1.47, v6 table -1.5, v5 table -1.7), so this record is labelled version 6. The definition sentences are the same on the v5 and v6 pages except for the ERSST version they name. Transcribed through two independent web-fetch reads of oni.ascii.txt (direct download was not available in the session), which agreed on every value.",
  "transcribed_by": "AI session (lane L2a loop, PR #310, seasons DJF 2000-NDJ 2025; printed values added and re-verified against both live sources by the L2a orchestrating session on 2026-11-15, two independent parsers agreeing)",
